---
source: crates/vps-ready/src/modules/net_tailscale/tests.rs
expression: plan
---
modules:
  - id: net.tailscale
    title: "Join a tailnet with Tailscale, for a private path to SSH"
    status: applicable
    changes:
      - id: "directory:/etc/apt/keyrings"
        summary: "create directory /etc/apt/keyrings (0755 0:0)"
        diff: ~
        reversibility: reversible
      - id: "file:/etc/apt/keyrings/tailscale.asc"
        summary: "create /etc/apt/keyrings/tailscale.asc (0644 0:0): PGP public key, fingerprint 2596 A99E AAB3 3821 893C 0A79 458C A832 957F 5868 (52 lines)"
        diff: ~
        reversibility: reversible
      - id: "file:/etc/apt/sources.list.d/tailscale.sources"
        summary: "create /etc/apt/sources.list.d/tailscale.sources (0644 0:0)"
        diff: "@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@\n+# Written by vps-ready. `vps-ready rollback --last` removes it.\n+Types: deb\n+URIs: https://pkgs.tailscale.com/stable/debian\n+Suites: trixie\n+Components: main\n+Architectures: amd64\n+Signed-By: /etc/apt/keyrings/tailscale.asc\n"
        reversibility: reversible
      - id: "file:/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52vps-ready-tailscale"
        summary: "create /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/52vps-ready-tailscale (0644 0:0)"
        diff: "@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\n+// Written by vps-ready (net.tailscale). `vps-ready rollback --last` removes it.\n+Unattended-Upgrade::Origins-Pattern { \"origin=Tailscale,codename=${distro_codename}\"; };\n"
        reversibility: reversible
      - id: "package:tailscale"
        summary: install tailscale
        diff: ~
        reversibility: partial
      - id: "service:tailscaled.service"
        summary: enable and start tailscaled.service
        diff: ~
        reversibility: reversible
      - id: "tailscale:up"
        summary: log in to the tailnet with the auth key in /root/tailscale-auth-key
        diff: ~
        reversibility: partial
    notes:
      - "no port is opened: Tailscale needs none, and firewall.inbound's established,related rule covers its replies; tailscaled's own nftables chains (ts-input) coexist with vps-ready's table"
      - delete /root/tailscale-auth-key after the login; a one-off key is spent once used
      - "rollback leaves Tailscale installed, with /var/lib/tailscale and the node's login, and removes the repository it updates from; `sudo tailscale logout` removes the node from the tailnet"
